{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To find the largest \\( x \\)-value at which the graphs of \\( f(x) \\) and \\( g(x) \\) intersect, we start by setting \\( f(x) = g(x) \\) and simplifying the equation.\n\nGiven:\n\\[ f(x) = e^{3x^2 - |\\lfloor x \\rfloor|!} + \\binom{22 + 735235|\\lfloor x \\rfloor|}{2356} + \\phi(|\\lfloor x \\rfloor| + 1) + 72x^4 + 3x^3 - 6x^2 + 2x + 1 \\]\n\\[ g(x) = e^{3x^2 - |\\lfloor x \\rfloor|!} + \\binom{22 + 735235|\\lfloor x \\rfloor|}{2356} + \\phi(|\\lfloor x \\rfloor| + 1) + 72x^4 + 4x^3 - 11x^2 - 6x + 13 \\]\n\nSubtract \\( g(x) \\) from \\( f(x) \\):\n\\[ f(x) - g(x) = (e^{3x^2 - |\\lfloor x \\rfloor|!} + \\binom{22 + 735235|\\lfloor x \\rfloor|}{2356} + \\phi(|\\lfloor x \\rfloor| + 1) + 72x^4 + 3x^3 - 6x^2 + 2x + 1) - (e^{3x^2 - |\\lfloor x \\rfloor|!} + \\binom{22 + 735235|\\lfloor x \\rfloor|}{2356} + \\phi(|\\lfloor x \\rfloor| + 1) + 72x^4 + 4x^3 - 11x^2 - 6x + 13) \\]\n\nSimplify the expression:\n\\[ f(x) - g(x) = (3x^3 - 6x^2 + 2x + 1) - (4x^3 - 11x^2 - 6x + 13) \\]\n\\[ f(x) - g(x) = 3x^3 - 6x^2 + 2x + 1 - 4x^3 + 11x^2 + 6x - 13 \\]\n\\[ f(x) - g(x) = -x^3 + 5x^2 + 8x - 12 \\]\n\nSet the simplified expression equal to zero:\n\\[ -x^3 + 5x^2 + 8x - 12 = 0 \\]\n\nTo find the roots of this polynomial, we use the Rational Root Theorem, which suggests that any rational root, \\( p/q \\), is a factor of the constant term (-12) divided by a factor of the leading coefficient (-1). The possible rational roots are \\( \\pm 1, \\pm 2, \\pm 3, \\pm 4, \\pm 6, \\pm 12 \\).\n\n","prefix_end":1411,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":false,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,1477,279,7772,17767,856,1124,7287,957,518,892,279,38999,315,17767,282,2075,8,1124,8,323,17767,342,2075,8,1124,8,31796,11,582,1191,553,6243,17767,282,2075,8,284,342,2075,8,1124,8,323,15491,7766,279,23606,382,22043,510,78045,282,2075,8,284,384,47822,18,87,61,17,481,63596,11008,3993,856,